READ ME - Morphospace

Morphospace.R is the code file used for the morphospace analyses in R.

Morpho.R is a script needed within Morphospace.R.

All .m files are package and script files needed for the analyses.

Code.m is the code file used to produce the morphospaces in MATLAB.

For all parts of the project the end of the file represents which part of the project it is used in:

None of the below - Fanning Method on Original Sample Size of 162
1 - Fanning Method on Increase Sample Size of 244
S - Swimming Method on Original Sample Size of 162
1S - Swimming Method on Increase Sample Size of 244

Image Files - Located within Images.zip. All files are named Genus_Species.tif.

Fish.csv - Column 1: List of species for which images are available. Column 2 & 3: First and Last appearance dates. As we are not using extinct species these columns are put to 0 as default. Column 4: Which group they belong to. By default 1 is non-fanning and 2 is fanning.

FishNames.csv - States the names of the groups for which column 4 in the Fish.csv file is numbered. Used for both Fish.csv and Fish1.csv. FishNamesSwimming.csv and FishNamesTest.csv are the same files corresponding to FishSwimming.csv and FishTest.csv.

Additionally FishVariation.csv and FishNamesVariation.csv were used to analyse the effect of intraspecific variation.

HarmonicArray.csv is produced in MATLAB and required in R.

FishData: Column 1 = Species Name. Column 2 = Fanning or Non-Fanning (No Care). Columns 3 & 4 = PC1 and PC2 values for each species from the generated morphospace for Fanning. Columns 5 & 6 = PC1 and PC2 values for each species from the generated morphospace for Swimming. Column 7 & 8 = Coded scores for Fanning (0 = Non-Fanning and 1 = Fanning) and Swimming (0 = Non-Pectoral Swimming, 1 = Pectoral Swimming and "-" = no data). The final column is just a checking column for the code. 
